1323..1394 Comment "/// Spinning a sum is composing the spins (cubical\'s `intLoop-hom`), by"
1395..1468 Comment "/// induction on the second summand. `spin` puts its new loop first where"
1469..1546 Comment "/// cubical\'s `intLoop` puts it last, so the law composes the spins the other"
1547..1608 Comment "/// way round, as the words compute: `(loop ∷ p) then q` is"
1609..1687 Comment "/// `loop ∷ (p then q)` (#422). At zero `spin(Z)` is a call that returns the"
1688..1762 Comment "/// empty word, and the composite over it runs that call first (#473); the"
1763..1834 Comment "/// composites the arms carry convert through their definitions (#440)."
